  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Strategic Partnership Arrangement - Phase 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Strategic Partnership Arrangement (SPA) Phase 3 is a trilateral arrangement between BRAC, Australia and Canada covering the period 2021-2026. In this Phase 3, Australia is providing for BRAC&apos;s development programs including, but not limited to, basic education, social protection, gender and skills programs that benefit millions of Bangladeshis, as well as support to BRAC&apos;s own institutional development. The SPA also supports BRAC&#x2019;s own organisational change agenda, helping BRAC to further develop its strategic approach and results reporting. The SPA represents the maturing of a relationship between BRAC and development partners from that of funder-implementer to the development of a partnership based on mutual trust, information sharing, and common development objectives. The total value of Australia&apos;s contribution is $85 million over 5 years, starting 2021-22.</narrative>
  </description>
